# discovery/php — PHP project scanning and launch

## Classes
| Class | Role |
| --- | --- |
| PhpProjectScanner | `composer.json` projects (Laravel/Symfony/PHP_COMPOSER) |
| StandalonePhpScanner | `index.php` without composer/package/pom |
| PhpLaunchCommands | Launch command builders + script selection apply |
| PhpComposerScripts | Filters runtime vs QA composer scripts |
| DockerComposeSupport | Detects compose files and published HTTP ports |

## Recognition rules
- Laravel: `artisan` or `laravel/framework`
- Symfony: `symfony.lock` / `bin/console` / symfony packages
- PHP_COMPOSER: runtime composer scripts **or** web docroot (`index.php`, `public/index.php`, `public/`)
- Legacy PHP with composer but no scripts is recognized when `index.php` exists at root
- Composer roots with only lint/test scripts and no web docroot are ignored

## Launch preference (`selectRuntimePhpScript`)
1. artisan:serve
2. composer `dev`/`serve`/`start`
3. docker:compose (when compose file present — ideal for Apache/PHP legacy stacks)
4. symfony:serve
5. php:serve (`php -S`, docroot `public` or `.`)

## Docker
- Script id: `docker:compose` → `docker compose up`
- Port read from compose preferred services (`app`/`web`/`php`/…)
- Skips host vendor check on start (entrypoint may run `composer install`)
